<!-- BEGIN SYSTEM LOCAL ELEVATION -->
## Local privilege elevation

For authorized local root operations on this box, use sudo with Navi phone approval:
`SUDO_ASKPASS=/bin/false script -q -E never -ec "sudo -A <exact command>" /dev/null < /dev/null`.
This is the explicit default across agentic development. The user approves each
command on the phone with a fingerprint. Do not use kdesu, pkexec, su, doas, or
other sudo forms as an automatic fallback. Keep ordinary development unprivileged
and preserve all tool sandbox and approval requirements; sandbox escalation alone
does not grant root. sudo returns the command's real exit status; a refused
approval prints "Not approved on the phone (rejected | timed out | phone
unreachable | busy)" with the request's own ID, and runs nothing. Retry a timeout
(never a rejection) up to three times, then stop and ask the user to say when they
are ready before resending. If the phone is unreachable, run the command once with
`SUDO_ASKPASS=/usr/bin/ksshaskpass sudo -A <exact command> < /dev/null` (password
dialog, no phone). Before the first
privileged action, read `ELEVATION.md` for command limits, output handling and
failure handling. Carry this rule into delegated work and resume after compaction.
<!-- END SYSTEM LOCAL ELEVATION -->
